(7668359, 1251032, 83313, '<td valign="top">I gave this an 8. Sorry to see it didn''t place higher, but abstract approaches tend to be less appreciated when not in an abstract specific challenge. Of course if the were in an abstract challenge, you''d get low voted because it was recognizable. Damned if ya do, damned if ya don''t.</td>', 'I gave this an 8. Sorry to see it didn''t place higher, but abstract approaches tend to be less appreciated when not in an abstract specific challenge. Of course if the were in an abstract challenge, you''d get low voted because it was recognizable. Damned if ya do, damned if ya don''t.', '2020-07-01 01:15:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(7668360, 1251098, 253313, '<td valign="top">Thanks Spiff for your comment. I cropped it close to accentuate the front of the vehicle.<br/>The picture was from the Miami Car Show years ago when I had a point and shoot camera. I just wanted to get something in the contest, trying to just get my feet wet,,being a newbie around here.<br/>Thanks again.<br/>Chuck</td>', 'Thanks Spiff for your comment. I cropped it close to accentuate the front of the vehicle.The picture was from the Miami Car Show years ago when I had a point and shoot camera. I just wanted to get something in the contest, trying to just get my feet wet,,being a newbie around here.Thanks again.Chuck', '2020-07-01 01:16:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(7668361, 1251098, 83313, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by crsteele:</b></div><hr/><i> Thanks Spiff for your comment. I cropped it close to accentuate the front of the vehicle.<br/>The picture was from the Miami Car Show years ago when I had a point and shoot camera. I just wanted to get something in the contest, trying to just get my feet wet,,being a newbie around here.<br/>Thanks again.<br/>Chuck </i></td></tr></table> <br/>You''re welcome. I''ve found a fast wideangle lens to be useful for these kind of public shows of things like cars and aircraft. Allows me to get close to block out the crowds, but still get the entire vehicle in. Now I''m thinking of other wideangle shots I could have entered of my own!</td>', 'Originally posted by crsteele: Thanks Spiff for your comment. I cropped it close to accentuate the front of the vehicle.The picture was from the Miami Car Show years ago when I had a point and shoot camera. I just wanted to get something in the contest, trying to just get my feet wet,,being a newbie around here.Thanks again.Chuck  You''re welcome. I''ve found a fast wideangle lens to be useful for these kind of public shows of things like cars and aircraft. Allows me to get close to block out the crowds, but still get the entire vehicle in. Now I''m thinking of other wideangle shots I could have entered of my own!', '2020-07-01 01:22:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(7668365, 1251237, 114285, '<td valign="top">I really love that vintage looking backdrop :-)</td>', 'I really love that vintage looking backdrop :-)', '2020-07-01 01:35:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(7668373, 1250936, 67145, '<td valign="top">wonderful photo Lydia .... congrats on the ribbon .. :)<br/> <br/><i>This is the tourist''s section of Havana. There were a bunch of tourists walking on the left that I got rid of (only in the photo... not in real life. Ha!). </i> <br/>btw .. this is the sort of thing i might have said .. ''not in real life'' .. we must have been separated at birth .. hahah .. ;)</td>', 'wonderful photo Lydia .... congrats on the ribbon .. :) This is the tourist''s section of Havana. There were a bunch of tourists walking on the left that I got rid of (only in the photo... not in real life. Ha!).  btw .. this is the sort of thing i might have said .. ''not in real life'' .. we must have been separated at birth .. hahah .. ;)', '2020-07-01 02:36:40.000000', NULL, 0),
